  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    H, W = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find block height by identifying the first row that is entirely the same color (separator)\n    bh = -1\n    for r in range(H):\n        if all(x == grid[r][0] for x in grid[r]):\n            bh = r\n            break\n            \n    # Find block width by identifying the first column that is entirely the same color (separator)\n    bw = -1\n    for c in range(W):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == grid[0][c] for r in range(H)):\n            bw = c\n            break\n            \n    if bh <= 0: bh = H\n    if bw <= 0: bw = W\n\n    out_H = (H + 1) // (bh + 1)\n    out_W = (W + 1) // (bw + 1)\n    \n    out_grid = []\n    for r in range(out_H):\n        row = []\n        for c in range(out_W):\n            # Extract the color of the subgrid (top-left pixel of each subgrid is sufficient)\n            row.append(grid[r * (bh + 1)][c * (bw + 1)])\n        # The pattern requires flipping the extracted grid horizontally\n        out_grid.append(row[::-1])\n        \n    return out_grid\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    H, W = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find block height by identifying the first row that is entirely the same color (separator)\n    bh = -1\n    for r in range(H):\n        if all(x == grid[r][0] for x in grid[r]):\n            bh = r\n            break\n            \n    # Find block width by identifying the first column that is entirely the same color (separator)\n    bw = -1\n    for c in range(W):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == grid[0][c] for r in range(H)):\n            bw = c\n            break\n            \n    if bh <= 0: bh = H\n    if bw <= 0: bw = W\n\n    out_H = (H + 1) // (bh + 1)\n    out_W = (W + 1) // (bw + 1)\n    \n    out_grid = []\n    for r in range(out_H):\n        row = []\n        for c in range(out_W):\n            # Extract the color of the subgrid (top-left pixel of each subgrid is sufficient)\n            row.append(grid[r * (bh + 1)][c * (bw + 1)])\n        # The pattern requires flipping the extracted grid horizontally\n        out_grid.append(row[::-1])\n        \n    return out_grid",
